{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115554",
      "title": "Component Inputs: Repetition",
      "lectureOrder": 101,
      "videoOrder": 95,
      "sourceHash": "da1642ab64b8bc5478295eea13b34011f499b577032fbf52f4bdb40ec9007537",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 2.61,
          "en": "So in order to reuse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.61,
          "end": 5.07,
          "en": "this dashboard item component as a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.07,
          "end": 8.49,
          "en": "for these specific dashboard item components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.49,
          "end": 11.4,
          "en": "we must make it more reusable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.4,
          "end": 15.45,
          "en": "Specifically, we must make sure that the image source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 20.45,
          "en": "the image alt, and this title here can be set from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.76,
          "end": 24.93,
          "en": "outside this dashboard item component, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.93,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "so that we can use this dashboard item component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 30.39,
          "en": "as a custom element in different places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 33.87,
          "en": "and then configure the concrete values of the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.87,
          "end": 36.45,
          "en": "of the alt text, and of the title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 38.724,
          "en": "depending on where we use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.724,
          "end": 41.97,
          "en": "And you did learn how you can make a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.97,
          "end": 46.97,
          "en": "reusable and configurable, you can add those inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.28,
          "end": 50.22,
          "en": "And therefore, here in this dashboard item component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.22,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "I want to accept two inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "One for the image, which should give me the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "for the image file and the alt text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 59.403,
          "en": "and one for the h2 tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.348,
          "end": 62.73,
          "en": "And you learned that there are two ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.73,
          "end": 65.49,
          "en": "of registering inputs in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.49,
          "end": 69.45,
          "en": "You can either use this input decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 70.98,
          "en": "or the input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 72.87,
          "en": "And I'll again show you both here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.87,
          "end": 75.51,
          "en": "so that you really are aware of both",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.51,
          "end": 78,
          "en": "because depending on the Angular version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 81.45,
          "en": "you are working with and the project you're working on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.45,
          "end": 83.88,
          "en": "you might be using different approaches,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.88,
          "end": 85.65299999999999,
          "en": "so you must know both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 88.89,
          "en": "So to register an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "an attribute of this custom component, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 95.16,
          "en": "you can use the @Input decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.16,
          "end": 98.88,
          "en": "followed by the name of the input you wanna accept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.88,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "And that name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 104.493,
          "en": "And it could, for example, be image for that image data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.65100000000001,
          "end": 108.50999999999999,
          "en": "Then, you should define the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.50999999999999,
          "end": 112.05,
          "en": "of data you expect to get here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.05,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "And I expect to get an object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 118.89,
          "en": "So that's now not an object value I'm creating,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.89,
          "end": 121.26,
          "en": "but since we're on the right side of the colon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.26,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "this now actually is an object type I'm defining.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 128.73,
          "en": "So I'm defining the shape of the object I expect to get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.73,
          "end": 131.343,
          "en": "as a value on that image property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.45,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "And I expect to get a property value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 139.77,
          "en": "which is an object which should have an SRC property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.77,
          "end": 141.84,
          "en": "though this of course is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 145.02,
          "en": "which should be of type string and an alt property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.02,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "which should also be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 151.173,
          "en": "So I expect to get such an object as a value for image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 155.31,
          "en": "In addition, this dashboard item component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.31,
          "end": 158.49,
          "en": "really only works if I do get image data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.49,
          "end": 163.07999999999998,
          "en": "and therefore image should actually be a required input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 166.02,
          "en": "And you also learned how you can tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.02,
          "end": 167.55,
          "en": "that it should be required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.55,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "You can pass an object to this input decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 173.94299999999998,
          "en": "and set required to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.07,
          "end": 179.43,
          "en": "And this will now tell Angular to throw an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.43,
          "end": 181.713,
          "en": "if that value should ever be omitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.94,
          "end": 184.2,
          "en": "Now since it is required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.2,
          "end": 186.42,
          "en": "we know that we will get the value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.42,
          "end": 189.12,
          "en": "and we can therefore add an exclamation mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.12,
          "end": 192.6,
          "en": "to tell TypeScript that this will never be undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 194.283,
          "en": "which it otherwise doesn't know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.66,
          "end": 198.06,
          "en": "Now, that's not the only input I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.06,
          "end": 202.598,
          "en": "Instead, I also want to get my title input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.598,
          "end": 206.94,
          "en": "and this should also be required here in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.94,
          "end": 209.52,
          "en": "So I'll set required to true here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.52,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "and add that exclamation mark.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 215.073,
          "en": "And here, I expect to get a simple string as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.227,
          "end": 219.63,
          "en": "Now alternatively, instead of using @Input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.63,
          "end": 222.66,
          "en": "you could also use that input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.66,
          "end": 225.9,
          "en": "In that case, I would still want a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 229.284,
          "en": "that's called image, an input that's called image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.284,
          "end": 231.84,
          "en": "But we'll turn this into an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.84,
          "end": 236.67000000000002,
          "en": "by assigning an initial value instead of using a decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.67000000000002,
          "end": 239.16,
          "en": "And that initial value is the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.16,
          "end": 241.937,
          "en": "of calling the input function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.937,
          "end": 246.51,
          "en": "which must be imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.51,
          "end": 249.48,
          "en": "Though this input function is only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.48,
          "end": 253.173,
          "en": "if you're using Angular 17.1 or later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.09,
          "end": 257.04,
          "en": "Now, when using this input function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 257.04,
          "end": 260.04,
          "en": "you can still mark image as a required input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.04,
          "end": 262.38,
          "en": "by adding a dot after the function name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.38,
          "end": 265.77,
          "en": "and calling required, so by using this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.77,
          "end": 268.8,
          "en": "that's defined on this function, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.8,
          "end": 270.33,
          "en": "And this then tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.33,
          "end": 272.973,
          "en": "that this should be a required input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.973,
          "end": 277.44,
          "en": "And of course, you can and should also still tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.44,
          "end": 281.283,
          "en": "which type of value will be received as an input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282.12,
          "end": 285.57,
          "en": "And here, you do that by using these angle brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.57,
          "end": 288.15,
          "en": "after input before the parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.15,
          "end": 292.26,
          "en": "or after required in this case, before the parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 292.26,
          "end": 294.39,
          "en": "And you then put your type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.39,
          "end": 296.193,
          "en": "between those angle brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.12,
          "end": 300.3,
          "en": "This is a so-called generic type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 300.3,
          "end": 303.87,
          "en": "or you're setting a generic type value to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.87,
          "end": 306.78,
          "en": "which here simply means that you give TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.78,
          "end": 310.2,
          "en": "extra information about which type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 310.2,
          "end": 312.543,
          "en": "the input will eventually receive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.95,
          "end": 316.47,
          "en": "Well and then we can also add the title input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.47,
          "end": 318.54,
          "en": "by using input.required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 318.54,
          "end": 320.733,
          "en": "And here, I expect to get a string.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
